// Muslim scriptures — 200+ verses from the Quran and Hadith with explanations.
// Rotates deterministically by day-of-year so no verse repeats for ~200 days.

export const MUSLIM_SCRIPTURES = [
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, with hardship comes ease. — Quran 94:6", scriptureExplanation: "This surah was revealed to reassure the Prophet during a time of difficulty. The promise isn't that hardship ends, but that ease comes alongside it — they coexist." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And whoever puts their trust in Allah, He will be enough for them. — Quran 65:3", scriptureExplanation: "Tawakkul (trust in God) is an active reliance, not passive waiting. The verse promises that God's sufficiency meets us when we place our dependence on Him." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "So remember Me; I will remember you. — Quran 2:152", scriptureExplanation: "This verse establishes a reciprocal relationship with God. Remembrance (dhikr) isn't just mental — it's an active practice that opens us to God's presence." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We have certainly created man in the best of stature. — Quran 95:4", scriptureExplanation: "This verse affirms human dignity. We are created with purpose and beauty — a reminder that our worth is not earned but given by our Creator." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And your Lord has decreed that you not worship except Him, and to parents, good treatment. — Quran 17:23", scriptureExplanation: "Kindness to parents is placed right after worship of God. This shows the importance of family in Islam — honoring parents is an act of faith." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins. — Quran 39:53", scriptureExplanation: "This verse is addressed to those who have sinned greatly. God's mercy is expansive — no one is beyond His forgiveness if they turn back to Him." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Verily, with the remembrance of Allah do hearts find rest. — Quran 13:28", scriptureExplanation: "This verse identifies the source of inner peace. True tranquility (sakina) comes not from circumstances but from connection with God." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And it is He who created the heavens and the earth in six days — and His Throne had been upon water. — Quran 11:7", scriptureExplanation: "This verse speaks to God's sovereignty over creation. The image of water — a source of life — reminds us that God's rule is life-giving, not oppressive." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And whoever fears Allah, He will make for him a way out. And will provide for him from where he does not expect. — Quran 65:2-3", scriptureExplanation: "Taqwa (God-consciousness) opens doors we can't see. The promise is both escape from difficulty and provision from unexpected sources." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "The most beloved of people to Allah are those who are most beneficial to people. — Hadith, reported by Tabarani", scriptureExplanation: "This hadith defines belovedness in terms of service. Being close to God is measured by how much good we do for others, not just our private worship." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. — Quran 1:1 (Al-Fatihah)", scriptureExplanation: "The opening of the Quran and every surah. God's names — Gracious and Merciful — frame everything that follows. His mercy precedes His judgment." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "All praise is for Allah, Lord of the worlds. — Quran 1:2", scriptureExplanation: "Praise is the starting point. God is Lord of all worlds — not just this one. Gratitude acknowledges His universal sovereignty." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. — Quran 1:3", scriptureExplanation: "God's mercy is emphasized twice. Ar-Rahman (universal mercy) and Ar-Raheem (specific mercy) — His compassion is both broad and personal." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Master of the Day of Judgment. — Quran 1:4", scriptureExplanation: "God is the Judge. This reminds us of accountability — but also of justice. The same God who is merciful is also just." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "You alone we worship, and You alone we ask for help. — Quran 1:5", scriptureExplanation: "Worship and help are both directed to God alone. This verse establishes tawhid (oneness) — our devotion and our dependence both belong to Him." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Guide us to the straight path. — Quran 1:6", scriptureExplanation: "Guidance is the primary request. Not wealth, not power — guidance. The straight path (sirat al-mustaqeem) is the way of those God has favored." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "The path of those upon whom You have bestowed favor, not of those who have evoked anger or of those who are astray. — Quran 1:7", scriptureExplanation: "The right path is defined by relationship. It's the way of those God has blessed — not the way of anger or error. Guidance is communal, not just individual." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Alif-Lam-Meem. This is the Book about which there is no doubt, a guidance for those conscious of Allah. — Quran 2:1-2", scriptureExplanation: "The Quran is guidance without doubt — for those with taqwa (God-consciousness). Certainty comes to the reverent, not the skeptical." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Who believe in the unseen, establish prayer, and spend out of what We have provided for them. — Quran 2:3", scriptureExplanation: "Faith, prayer, and charity define the believer. Belief in the unseen, regular prayer, and generosity — these are the marks of a God-conscious life." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And who believe in what has been revealed to you and what was revealed before you, and of the Hereafter they are certain. — Quran 2:4", scriptureExplanation: "Faith includes all revelation and the Hereafter. Belief is not selective — it embraces all of God's messages and the certainty of eternity." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Those are upon guidance from their Lord, and it is those who are successful. — Quran 2:5", scriptureExplanation: "Guidance leads to success. The God-conscious are on the right path — and true success (falah) is spiritual, not just material." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, those who disbelieve — it is all the same for them whether you warn them or do not warn them — they will not believe. — Quran 2:6", scriptureExplanation: "Some hearts are closed. Warning doesn't always produce faith — but our job is to warn, not to force. Results belong to God." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Allah has set a seal upon their hearts and upon their hearing, and over their vision is a veil. — Quran 2:7", scriptureExplanation: "Persistent rejection has consequences. God seals what was already closed — the heart that refuses truth eventually loses the capacity to receive it." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And of the people are some who say, 'We believe in Allah and the Last Day,' but they are not believers. — Quran 2:8", scriptureExplanation: "True belief is more than words. Claiming faith without living it is not belief — sincerity (ikhlas) is the test of genuine faith." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "They seek to deceive Allah and those who believe, but they deceive not except themselves and perceive it not. — Quran 2:9", scriptureExplanation: "Self-deception is the deepest deception. Those who pretend faith fool only themselves — God is never deceived. Honesty starts with the self." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "In their hearts is disease, so Allah has increased their disease; and for them is a painful punishment. — Quran 2:10", scriptureExplanation: "Spiritual disease worsens without treatment. Hypocrisy is a sickness — and ignoring it makes it worse. The cure is sincerity." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And when it is said to them, 'Do not cause corruption on the earth,' they say, 'We are but reformers.' — Quran 2:11", scriptureExplanation: "Wrongdoing often disguises itself as reform. The corrupt call themselves peacemakers — self-deception rationalizes harm. True reform starts with honesty." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Unquestionably, it is they who are the corrupters, but they perceive it not. — Quran 2:12", scriptureExplanation: "The corrupt don't see their corruption. Blindness to one's own wrongdoing is the deepest form of damage — awareness is the first step to change." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And when it is said to them, 'Believe as the people have believed,' they say, 'Should we believe as the foolish have believed?' — Quran 2:13", scriptureExplanation: "Arrogance rejects faith. The hypocrite calls believers foolish — pride prevents them from humbling themselves to receive truth." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Unquestionably, it is they who are the foolish, but they know it not. — Quran 2:14", scriptureExplanation: "The foolish think themselves wise. True wisdom includes knowing what you don't know — the arrogant are blind to their own ignorance." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And when they meet those who believe, they say, 'We believe'; but when they are alone with their evil ones, they say, 'Indeed, we are with you.' — Quran 2:14 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Double-faced faith is no faith. Saying one thing to believers and another to enemies reveals a divided heart — integrity is consistency." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Allah mocks them and prolongs them in their transgression, wandering blindly. — Quran 2:15", scriptureExplanation: "God allows the hypocrite to continue in their path. Prolonged error is its own punishment — the freedom to stray is also the freedom to suffer." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Those are the ones who have purchased error in exchange for guidance, so their transaction has brought no profit, nor were they guided. — Quran 2:16", scriptureExplanation: "Trading guidance for error is a losing deal. The hypocrite exchanged truth for falsehood — and gained nothing. The cost of compromise is total." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Their example is that of one who kindled a fire, but when it illuminated what was around him, Allah took away their light and left them in darkness, unable to see. — Quran 2:17", scriptureExplanation: "False light is temporary. The hypocrite's faith illuminates briefly, then God removes it — leaving darkness. Genuine faith is lasting light." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Deaf, dumb, and blind, so they will not return. — Quran 2:18", scriptureExplanation: "Spiritual senses can be lost. Deaf to truth, mute in praise, blind to guidance — the persistent hypocrite loses the capacity to return. Awareness is precious." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Or like a rainstorm from the sky within which is darkness, thunder, and lightning. — Quran 2:19", scriptureExplanation: "Faith without roots is unstable. Like a person in a storm — the hypocrite is overwhelmed by life's trials because their faith has no foundation." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "They put their fingers in their ears against the thunderclaps in fear of death. But Allah is encompassing of the disbelievers. — Quran 2:19 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Fear drives the hypocrite. They fear creation instead of the Creator — but God encompasses everything, including their fear." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "The lightning almost snatches away their sight. Every time it lights for them, they walk therein; but when darkness comes over them, they stand still. — Quran 2:20", scriptureExplanation: "Convenience defines hypocritical faith. When it's easy, they walk; when it's hard, they stop. True faith walks in both light and darkness." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And if Allah had willed, He could have taken away their hearing and their sight. Indeed, Allah is over all things competent. — Quran 2:20 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "God's power is absolute. He could remove even the senses of the hypocrite — His competence extends over all things, including human faculties." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "O mankind, worship your Lord, who created you and those before you, that you may become righteous. — Quran 2:21", scriptureExplanation: "Worship leads to righteousness. God created us — and worship is the path to taqwa. Devotion is not just duty; it's transformation." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "He who made for you the earth a bed and the sky a ceiling and sent down from the sky rain and brought forth thereby fruits as provision for you. — Quran 2:22", scriptureExplanation: "God provides through creation. The earth as a bed, the sky as a ceiling, rain as provision — God's care is built into the very structure of the world." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "So do not set up rivals to Allah while you know. — Quran 2:22b", scriptureExplanation: "Knowing God should end idolatry. When we truly know the Creator, setting up rivals becomes absurd — knowledge leads to exclusive devotion." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And if you are in doubt about what We have sent down upon Our Servant, then produce a surah like it. — Quran 2:23", scriptureExplanation: "The Quran is inimitable. God challenges doubters to match it — the challenge stands unanswered. The text itself is evidence of divine origin." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But if you do not — and you will never — then fear the Fire, whose fuel is men and stones, prepared for the disbelievers. — Quran 2:24", scriptureExplanation: "The challenge is certain. 'You will never' — God's confidence is absolute. The consequence of persistent disbelief is severe." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And give good tidings to those who believe and do righteous deeds that for them will be gardens beneath which rivers flow. — Quran 2:25", scriptureExplanation: "Paradise is for the believing doer. Faith and action together — not one without the other. The reward is a garden, a place of life and beauty." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Whenever they are provided with fruit therefrom, they say, 'This is what we were provided with before.' — Quran 2:25 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Paradise is familiar yet ever-new. The fruit is recognized but always fresh — eternity is not boring but endlessly delightful." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And they will have therein purified spouses, and they will abide therein eternally. — Quran 2:25b", scriptureExplanation: "Paradise includes relationship and permanence. Purified spouses and eternal dwelling — the reward is both relational and lasting." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, Allah is not timid to present an example — that of a mosquito or what is smaller than it. — Quran 2:26", scriptureExplanation: "God uses small things to teach big truths. Even a mosquito can illustrate divine reality — God is not limited by the size of His illustrations." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Those who have believed know that it is the truth from their Lord, but those who disbelieve say, 'What did Allah intend by this example?' — Quran 2:26 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "The same example divides hearts. Believers see truth; doubters question God's purpose. The same word produces different responses depending on the heart." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "He misleads many thereby and guides many thereby. And He misleads not thereby except the defiantly disobedient. — Quran 2:26b", scriptureExplanation: "Guidance and misguidance both come through God's word. The defiant are misled; the humble are guided. Our posture toward God determines the effect of His word." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Who break the covenant of Allah after contracting it and sever what Allah has ordered to be joined and cause corruption on earth. — Quran 2:27", scriptureExplanation: "Three marks of the lost: breaking covenants, severing relationships, spreading corruption. Faithfulness, connection, and care are the opposites." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "It is those who are the losers. — Quran 2:27b", scriptureExplanation: "True loss is spiritual. The one who breaks covenant and spreads corruption is the real loser — not the one who suffers, but the one who sins." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "How can you disbelieve in Allah when you were lifeless and He brought you to life; then He will cause you to die, then He will bring you to life. — Quran 2:28", scriptureExplanation: "God gives life twice — physical and spiritual. Creation and resurrection are both His. Disbelief ignores the most basic fact: God is the source of life." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Then to Him you will be returned. — Quran 2:28b", scriptureExplanation: "Return is certain. We came from God and we go back to Him — this is the fundamental fact of existence. Accountability is built in." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "It is He who created for you all that the earth contains, then He turned to the heaven and made them seven heavens. — Quran 2:29", scriptureExplanation: "Creation is for us. Everything on earth was created for humanity — not as an accident but as a gift. The universe is intentional." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And He is Knowing of all things. — Quran 2:29b", scriptureExplanation: "God's knowledge is total. He knows creation, humanity, and every detail — nothing surprises Him. His omniscience is our security." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And when your Lord said to the angels, 'I will make on the earth a khalifah.' — Quran 2:30", scriptureExplanation: "Humanity is God's representative. Khalifah means steward — we're placed on earth to represent God's rule. Dignity comes with responsibility." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "They said, 'Will You place upon it one who causes corruption and sheds blood, while we declare Your praise and sanctify You?' — Quran 2:30 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "The angels questioned humanity's role. They saw our potential for harm — but God saw more. His wisdom exceeds even angelic understanding." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Allah said, 'Indeed, I know that which you do not know.' — Quran 2:30b", scriptureExplanation: "God's knowledge exceeds all. Even angels don't know what God knows — His plan includes what we can't see. Trust His wisdom over our questions." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And He taught Adam the names — all of them. — Quran 2:31", scriptureExplanation: "Knowledge is humanity's gift. God taught Adam what even angels didn't know — knowledge is part of our divine endowment. We're made to learn." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Then He showed them to the angels and said, 'Inform Me of the names of these, if you are truthful.' — Quran 2:31 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "God tested the angels. He asked them to name what they couldn't — demonstrating that human knowledge, given by God, surpasses angelic knowledge." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "They said, 'Exalted are You; we have no knowledge except what You have taught us. Indeed, it is You who is the Knowing, the Wise.' — Quran 2:32", scriptureExplanation: "The angels acknowledged their limits. True knowledge begins with humility — 'we have no knowledge except what You taught us.' Wisdom starts with admitting what we don't know." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "He said, 'O Adam, inform them of the names.' And when he had informed them, He said, 'Did I not tell you that I know the unseen of the heavens and the earth?' — Quran 2:33", scriptureExplanation: "Adam's knowledge confirmed God's word. God's knowledge includes the unseen — and He shares it with whom He wills. Revelation flows from omniscience." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And I know what you reveal and what you have concealed. — Quran 2:33b", scriptureExplanation: "God sees the hidden. What we show and what we hide are both visible to Him — nothing is truly secret. This is both warning and comfort." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And when We said to the angels, 'Prostrate before Adam'; so they prostrated, except for Iblees. — Quran 2:34", scriptureExplanation: "Even angels bowed to humanity. God honored Adam above angels — except Iblees, whose pride refused. Humility vs. pride is the first spiritual divide." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "He refused and was arrogant and became of the disbelievers. — Quran 2:34b", scriptureExplanation: "Pride leads to disbelief. Iblees's refusal wasn't ignorance — it was arrogance. The first sin was not an action but an attitude: refusing to bow." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We said, 'O Adam, dwell, you and your wife, in Paradise and eat therefrom in abundance from wherever you will.' — Quran 2:35", scriptureExplanation: "Paradise was humanity's first home. Abundance and freedom were the original plan — God's intention was provision, not deprivation." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But do not approach this tree, lest you be among the wrongdoers. — Quran 2:35b", scriptureExplanation: "Freedom has a boundary. One tree, one limit — not to restrict joy but to test trust. Obedience in abundance is the test of gratitude." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But Satan caused them to slip out of it and removed them from that condition in which they had been. — Quran 2:36", scriptureExplanation: "Satan's goal is removal. He doesn't create new desires — he exploits existing ones to remove us from our God-given condition. Vigilance is needed." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We said, 'Go down, all of you, as enemies to one another. And you will have upon the earth a place of settlement and provision for a time.' — Quran 2:36 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Earth is a temporary home with provision. The fall brought enmity and mortality — but also a place to live and provision to sustain. Exile is not abandonment." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Then Adam received from his Lord words, and He accepted his repentance. Indeed, it is He who is the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful. — Quran 2:37", scriptureExplanation: "Repentance is always accepted. Adam sinned, repented, and was forgiven — God's mercy follows genuine return. He is the Accepting of repentance (Tawwab)." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "We said, 'Go down from it, all of you. And when guidance comes to you from Me, whoever follows My guidance — there will be no fear concerning them, nor will they grieve.' — Quran 2:38", scriptureExplanation: "Guidance removes fear. Following God's guidance leads to a life without fear or grief — not because trouble disappears, but because trust replaces terror." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And those who disbelieve and deny Our signs — those are companions of the Fire; they will abide therein eternally. — Quran 2:39", scriptureExplanation: "Persistent disbelief has consequences. Denying God's signs leads to separation — but the door of repentance remains open until the end." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "O Children of Israel, remember My favor which I have bestowed upon you and fulfill My covenant. — Quran 2:40", scriptureExplanation: "Remembering God's favors is a duty. Gratitude for past blessings fuels present faithfulness — memory of God's goodness sustains obedience." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And fear a Day when no soul shall avail another. — Quran 2:48", scriptureExplanation: "Each person answers for themselves. No one can carry another's burden — individual accountability is absolute. This sobers us into personal responsibility." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And seek help through patience and prayer. — Quran 2:45a", scriptureExplanation: "Patience (sabr) and prayer (salah) are the two tools for difficult times. Together they sustain us — endurance in action and connection in worship." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And indeed, it is difficult except upon the humble. — Quran 2:45b", scriptureExplanation: "Prayer is hard for the proud. Humility makes worship natural — the humble find prayer a joy, not a burden. Pride is the obstacle to devotion." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Who are certain that they will meet their Lord and that they will return to Him. — Quran 2:46", scriptureExplanation: "Certainty of meeting God transforms prayer. When we know we'll face Him, worship becomes preparation — not performance, but encounter." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "O Children of Israel, remember My favor which I have bestowed upon you and that I favored you over the worlds. — Quran 2:47", scriptureExplanation: "God's favor is remembered. Israel was chosen — not because of merit but because of grace. Remembering favor fuels gratitude and faithfulness." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And fear a Day when no soul will suffice for another soul at all, and no intercession will be accepted from it, nor any compensation taken from it, nor will they be aided. — Quran 2:48 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Ultimate accountability. No proxy, no bribe, no helper — each soul stands alone before God. This should drive us to prepare now, not later." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We delivered the Children of Israel from the humiliating torment. — Quran 2:49", scriptureExplanation: "God rescues His people. The Exodus is recalled — God delivered Israel from Pharaoh. He is the same God who delivers us today." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "From Pharaoh and his people, who were afflicting them with severe torment. — Quran 2:49 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Oppression is real. God sees the affliction of His people — and He acts. The same God who freed Israel can free us from our Pharaohs." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We made the people who were considered weak to inherit the eastern and western portions of the land. — Quran 2:50a", scriptureExplanation: "God elevates the lowly. The weak inherited the land — God's pattern is to lift the humble and humble the proud. His economy reverses the world's." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We made the oppressed children of Israel leaders. — Quran 2:50b", scriptureExplanation: "Oppression can lead to leadership. God turned slaves into leaders — the same can happen to us. Our suffering may be preparation for responsibility." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And Moses said to his people, 'O my people, remember the favor of Allah upon you when He made among you prophets and made you kings.' — Quran 5:20", scriptureExplanation: "Gratitude for past blessings fuels present courage. Moses reminded Israel of God's favors — remembering what God has done gives strength for what's ahead." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And He gave you from all you asked of Him. — Quran 14:34a", scriptureExplanation: "God answers abundantly. Every good thing we have comes from Him — gratitude is the appropriate response to His generosity." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And if you should count the favor of Allah, you could not enumerate them. — Quran 14:34b", scriptureExplanation: "God's blessings are uncountable. We can't even list them all — and yet we often focus on what we lack. Gratitude starts with recognizing abundance." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, mankind is unjust and ungrateful. — Quran 14:34c", scriptureExplanation: "Ingratitude is our default. We minimize God's gifts and magnify our problems — awareness of this tendency is the first step toward gratitude." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And when your Lord proclaimed: 'If you are grateful, I will surely increase you; but if you are ungrateful, indeed, My punishment is severe.' — Quran 14:7", scriptureExplanation: "Gratitude leads to increase. God multiplies what we appreciate — ingratitude leads to loss. Thankfulness is not just polite; it's productive." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And Allah is the Free of need, the Praiseworthy. — Quran 14:8", scriptureExplanation: "God needs nothing. Our worship doesn't add to Him — but our gratitude transforms us. He is praiseworthy regardless of our response." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We have certainly honored the children of Adam and carried them on the land and sea and provided for them of the good things. — Quran 17:70", scriptureExplanation: "Humanity is honored. God has dignified us — providing good things, carrying us across land and sea. Honor is God's gift to all people." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We have preferred them over much of what We have created. — Quran 17:70b", scriptureExplanation: "Humans are privileged. God has given us preference over much of creation — dignity is not earned but bestowed. Worth comes from the Creator." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And do not pursue that of which you have no knowledge. Indeed, the hearing, the sight, and the heart — all of those will be questioned. — Quran 17:36", scriptureExplanation: "Accountability for senses. What we hear, see, and feel will be questioned — we're responsible for our input, not just our output. Guard your gates." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And do not walk upon the earth exultantly. Indeed, you will not tear the earth, and you will not reach the mountains in height. — Quran 17:37", scriptureExplanation: "Arrogance is absurd. We can't split the earth or reach the mountains — pride is disproportionate to our actual power. Humility is realism." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "The evil of that is hated by your Lord. — Quran 17:38", scriptureExplanation: "God detests arrogance. What we celebrate, God hates — self-importance is not just unwise but offensive to Him. Humility is what He loves." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "This is of what your Lord has revealed to you of wisdom. — Quran 17:39a", scriptureExplanation: "Wisdom is revealed. It comes from God, not from within — we receive it, we don't generate it. Revelation is the source of true understanding." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And do not make with Allah another deity, lest you be thrown into Hell, blamed and banished. — Quran 17:39b", scriptureExplanation: "Tawhid is the foundation. One God — not many. Polytheism leads to Hell, blamed and banished. Oneness is not just theology; it's salvation." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Then is he who is a believer like him who is defiantly disobedient? They are not equal. — Quran 32:18", scriptureExplanation: "Faith changes everything. The believer and the disobedient are not the same — their paths, their ends, their peace are all different. Faith matters." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "As for those who believed and did righteous deeds, for them are the Gardens of Refuge as accommodation for what they used to do. — Quran 32:19", scriptureExplanation: "Paradise is earned through faith and action. Not by belief alone, not by works alone — both together. The reward matches the life." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But as for those who defiantly disobeyed, their refuge is the Fire. Every time they wish to come out of it, they are returned. — Quran 32:20", scriptureExplanation: "Persistent rebellion has a destination. The Fire is not temporary for the defiant — they try to leave but are returned. Choices have permanent consequences." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We will let them taste the lesser punishment before the greater punishment, that perhaps they may return. — Quran 32:21", scriptureExplanation: "Lesser trials are invitations. Hardship in this life can be a wake-up call — God sends smaller pains to prevent greater ones. Repentance is the goal." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And who is more unjust than one who is reminded of the verses of his Lord and then turns away from them? — Quran 32:22", scriptureExplanation: "Ignoring revelation is the worst injustice. To hear God's word and turn away — there's no greater rejection. The informed have greater accountability." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, Allah is with those who fear Him and those who are doers of good. — Quran 16:128", scriptureExplanation: "God's company is conditional. He is with the God-conscious and the good-doers — not just the believers in name. Presence follows practice." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And do not extend your eyes toward that by which We have given enjoyment to certain categories of them. — Quran 15:88", scriptureExplanation: "Don't envy others' provision. What God gives to some is a test for them — and a test for us. Looking at what others have breeds discontent." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And do not be grieved over them, and lower your wing over the believers. — Quran 15:88b", scriptureExplanation: "Don't grieve over the proud. Instead, be tender with the believers — 'lower your wing' is an image of gentleness. Care for the faithful, not the defiant." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And say, 'Indeed, I am the clear warner.' — Quran 15:89", scriptureExplanation: "Warning is a duty. We're to warn clearly — not to force, but to inform. The messenger's job is clarity, not conversion." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, your Lord is the best of creators. — Quran 23:14", scriptureExplanation: "God is the supreme Creator. His creation is the best — and we are His work. Dignity comes from being made by the best of creators." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Then We made the sperm-drop into a clinging clot, and We made the clot into a lump, and We made the lump into bones, and We covered the bones with flesh. — Quran 23:14 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Creation is staged. God's work is gradual — each stage building on the last. Growth is God's pattern, both in the womb and in the soul." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Then We developed him into another creation. So blessed is Allah, the best of creators. — Quran 23:14b", scriptureExplanation: "We are a new creation. God's final work in us is transformation — from flesh to spirit. The best of creators makes us new." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Then indeed, after that you are to die. — Quran 23:15", scriptureExplanation: "Death is certain. No one escapes it — the question is not if but when. Awareness of death shapes how we live." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Then indeed, on the Day of Resurrection you will be resurrected. — Quran 23:16", scriptureExplanation: "Resurrection follows death. The grave is not the end — we will be raised. This life is preparation for the next." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We have created above you seven layered heavens, and not unaware of creation. — Quran 23:17", scriptureExplanation: "God's creation is vast and intentional. Seven heavens — and God is not unaware of any of it. His sovereignty extends over all." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We sent down from the sky water in measure, and We gave it lodging in the earth. — Quran 23:18", scriptureExplanation: "God's provision is measured. Rain comes in due measure — not too much, not too little. God's provision is perfectly calibrated." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And indeed, We are able to take it away. — Quran 23:18b", scriptureExplanation: "God can withdraw provision. The rain we depend on is His gift — and He can take it back. Gratitude includes recognizing our dependence." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Then We brought forth for you thereby gardens of palm trees and grapevines. — Quran 23:19", scriptureExplanation: "God's provision is beautiful. From water come gardens — beauty is part of God's design. He doesn't just sustain; He delights." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "In which is for you abundant fruit and from which you eat. — Quran 23:19b", scriptureExplanation: "Fruit is for eating. God's provision is meant to be enjoyed — not just admired. Pleasure is part of His plan." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And a tree from Mount Sinai that produces oil and seasoning for those who eat. — Quran 23:20", scriptureExplanation: "Even the olive is a gift. From a specific mountain comes a specific blessing — God's provision is both general and particular." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And indeed, for you in livestock is a lesson. — Quran 23:21", scriptureExplanation: "Animals teach us. Creation is a classroom — even livestock have lessons. Observation of the natural world leads to spiritual insight." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "We give you drink from what is in their bellies, and for you in them are numerous benefits. — Quran 23:21 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Even animal products are provision. Milk, transport, clothing — God provides through animals. Every good thing has a source in God's design." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We have certainly sent Noah to his people, and he said, 'O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him.' — Quran 23:23", scriptureExplanation: "The message is always the same. From Noah to Muhammad — worship God alone. The core of prophetic teaching never changes." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "So fear Allah and obey me. — Quran 23:23b", scriptureExplanation: "Fear and obedience go together. Taqwa leads to following the messenger — reverence produces action. Faith is not just belief but obedience." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And the eminent among his people who disbelieved said, 'This is not but a man like yourselves who seeks to make himself superior to you.' — Quran 23:24", scriptureExplanation: "Pride rejects the messenger. The powerful dismissed Noah as an ambitious man — status blinds people to truth. The humble hear; the proud dismiss." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But if Allah had willed, He would have sent down angels. — Quran 23:24b", scriptureExplanation: "God could have sent angels. But He chose humans to guide humans — relatability is part of the plan. The messenger is one of us." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "We have not heard of this in the former religion. — Quran 23:24c", scriptureExplanation: "Novelty doesn't mean falsehood. The disbelievers rejected Noah's message as new — but truth can be new to those who haven't heard it. Familiarity is not the test of truth." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "This is not but a fabrication. — Quran 23:25", scriptureExplanation: "Dismissal is the easy response. Rather than engage, the proud label truth as fabrication — rejection is simpler than reflection." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Said the eminent ones who disbelieved among his people, 'We do not believe you.' — Quran 23:26a", scriptureExplanation: "Status doesn't guarantee wisdom. The leaders rejected Noah — authority and truth are not the same. The majority can be wrong." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "So he invoked his Lord, 'I am overpowered, so help.' — Quran 23:39", scriptureExplanation: "When overwhelmed, call on God. Noah didn't fight back — he prayed. Helplessness is the right posture before divine power." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, the Hour is coming, so forgive with gracious forgiveness. — Quran 15:85", scriptureExplanation: "Forgive because the end is near. The awareness of the Hour softens our response to others — gracious forgiveness reflects God's own mercy." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, your Lord — He who creates and He who knows. — Quran 15:86", scriptureExplanation: "God both creates and knows. He made us and understands us — His knowledge is not detached but intimate. The Creator knows His creation." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We have certainly given you seven of the often repeated and the great Quran. — Quran 15:87", scriptureExplanation: "The seven often-repeated are Al-Fatihah. God gave the greatest surah — recited in every prayer. The foundation of prayer is a gift." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Do not extend your eyes toward what We have given to some categories of them. — Quran 15:88 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Don't covet. What others have is their test, not your reward. Eyes that wander breed discontent — focus on your own path." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And do not grieve over them, and lower your wing to the believers. — Quran 15:88b (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Tenderness to the faithful. Don't waste grief on the proud — pour gentleness on believers. The wing lowered is the wing that protects." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And say, 'Indeed, I am the clear warner.' — Quran 15:89 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Clarity is a duty. We're to warn clearly — not to coerce, but to inform. The messenger's role is transparency, not control." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, Allah does not change the condition of a people until they change what is in themselves. — Quran 13:11", scriptureExplanation: "Change starts within. God transforms circumstances when we transform our hearts — external change follows internal change. Repentance precedes renewal." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And when harm touches man, he invokes Us, lying on his side or sitting or standing. — Quran 10:12", scriptureExplanation: "We pray when we're desperate. In hardship, we turn to God — but often forget Him in ease. Consistent prayer, not just crisis prayer, is the goal." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But when We remove the harm from him, he continues in his way as if he had never invoked Us. — Quran 10:12b", scriptureExplanation: "Forgetfulness after rescue. We cry for help, then forget the Helper — ingratitude is our default. Remembering God in ease is the test of gratitude." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Thus is made pleasing to the transgressors that which they have been doing. — Quran 10:12c", scriptureExplanation: "Sin looks good to the sinner. Wrongdoing is made attractive — the transgressor doesn't see the ugliness of their own actions. Deception is part of the test." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And if We had made it a Quran in a foreign language, they would have said, 'Why are its verses not explained in detail?' — Quran 41:44", scriptureExplanation: "People find reasons to reject. Even a foreign-language Quran would be dismissed — the issue is not the message but the heart. Excuses reveal resistance." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Say, 'It is, for those who believe, a guidance and a healing.' — Quran 41:44b", scriptureExplanation: "The Quran heals. For believers, it's both guidance and medicine — it directs and it cures. The word of God is therapeutic." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But those who are blind — in their hearts is a disease. — Quran 41:44c (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Spiritual blindness is a disease. The Quran can heal — but only for those who believe. The same sun that melts wax hardens clay." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We have certainly presented for mankind in this Quran every example. — Quran 30:58", scriptureExplanation: "The Quran is comprehensive. Every kind of example is given — no one is left without guidance. The message is complete." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But man has not been except disputatious. — Quran 30:58b", scriptureExplanation: "We love to argue. Even with complete guidance, humans find reasons to dispute — argument is often a cover for resistance." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "So be patient. Indeed, the promise of Allah is truth. — Quran 30:60", scriptureExplanation: "Patience is rooted in promise. God's word is true — so we can wait. The certainty of His promise sustains us through delay." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And let not those who have no certainty avert you. — Quran 30:60b", scriptureExplanation: "Don't let doubters distract you. Those without faith will try to shake yours — stay steady. Certainty is contagious; so is doubt. Choose your influences." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And of His signs is that He created for you from yourselves mates that you may find tranquility in them. — Quran 30:21", scriptureExplanation: "Marriage is a sign of God. Tranquility (sakinah) in a spouse is a divine gift — relationships are not just social but spiritual. Love is a sign." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And He placed between you affection and mercy. — Quran 30:21b", scriptureExplanation: "Love and mercy in marriage are from God. Affection (mawaddah) and mercy (rahmah) — both are divine deposits. Lasting relationships need both." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed in that are signs for a people who give thought. — Quran 30:21c", scriptureExplanation: "Reflection reveals signs. God's fingerprints are everywhere — but only the thoughtful see them. Contemplation is the key to wonder." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And of His signs is the creation of the heavens and the earth and the diversity of your languages and colors. — Quran 30:22", scriptureExplanation: "Diversity is a sign. Different languages and colors are not accidental but intentional — variety reveals God's creativity. Difference is divine design." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed in that are signs for those of knowledge. — Quran 30:22b", scriptureExplanation: "Knowledge reveals signs. The learned see what the ignorant miss — study deepens wonder. Education is a form of worship." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And of His signs is your sleep by night and day and your seeking of His bounty. — Quran 30:23", scriptureExplanation: "Rest and work are both signs. Sleep and labor — both are from God. The rhythm of life is His design." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed in that are signs for a people who listen. — Quran 30:23b", scriptureExplanation: "Listening reveals signs. Those who truly hear — not just with ears but with hearts — perceive God's messages in daily life." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And of His signs is that He shows you the lightning as fear and hope. — Quran 30:24", scriptureExplanation: "Even weather is a sign. Lightning brings both fear (of its danger) and hope (of rain) — God's creation evokes both reverence and expectation." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And He sends down rain from the sky by which He brings to life the earth after its lifelessness. — Quran 30:24b", scriptureExplanation: "Rain revives. God brings life from death — the dead earth becomes green. This is a picture of spiritual resurrection." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed in that are signs for a people who use their reason. — Quran 30:24c", scriptureExplanation: "Reason reveals signs. Thinking — not just feeling — leads to God. The intellect is a pathway to wonder." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And of His signs is that the heavens and the earth stand by His command. — Quran 30:25", scriptureExplanation: "The universe is sustained by God's word. It doesn't run on autopilot — His command holds it together. Every moment of existence is an act of God." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Then when He calls you with a single call from the earth, immediately you will come forth. — Quran 30:25b", scriptureExplanation: "Resurrection is instant. One call — and we emerge. The speed of God's command shows His power. What seems impossible to us is effortless to Him." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And to Him belongs whoever is in the heavens and the earth. All are to Him devoutly obedient. — Quran 30:26", scriptureExplanation: "Everything obeys God. The whole cosmos is devoted to Him — except humans, who have a choice. Our obedience is meaningful because it's voluntary." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And it is He who begins creation; then He repeats it. — Quran 30:27a", scriptureExplanation: "God creates and recreates. The first creation proves the second — if He can make us once, He can make us again. Resurrection is logical." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And that is easier for Him. — Quran 30:27b", scriptureExplanation: "Resurrection is easy for God. What we find impossible, He finds simple — our limitations are not His. Trust His power." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And to Him is the highest attribute in the heavens and the earth. — Quran 30:27c", scriptureExplanation: "God's attributes are supreme. Nothing compares to Him — His qualities are the highest. Worship is the fitting response to His perfection." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And He is the Exalted in Might, the Wise. — Quran 30:27d", scriptureExplanation: "God is both mighty and wise. Power without wisdom is dangerous; wisdom without power is helpless. God has both — and both are perfect." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "He presents to you an example from yourselves: Do you have among those whom your right hands possess any partners in what We have provided for you? — Quran 30:28", scriptureExplanation: "God uses familiar examples. He teaches through what we already know — partnership in provision — to explain His oneness. Teaching starts with the known." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "So you are of Him fearing, as you fear one another. — Quran 30:28b", scriptureExplanation: "Fear of God should match our fear of each other — but it should exceed it. God is greater than any human we might fear." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Thus do We detail the signs for a people who use reason. — Quran 30:28c", scriptureExplanation: "Signs are detailed for thinkers. God doesn't just give signs — He explains them. Understanding requires both revelation and reason." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But those who wrong follow their desires without knowledge. — Quran 30:29a", scriptureExplanation: "Wrongdoing follows desire, not knowledge. The wrongdoer is led by want, not wisdom — desire without knowledge is destructive." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Then who can guide one whom Allah has sent astray? — Quran 30:29b", scriptureExplanation: "Once God withdraws guidance, none can restore it. This is a warning — don't persist in error until guidance is removed. Repent while the door is open." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And for them will not be any helpers. — Quran 30:29c", scriptureExplanation: "The misguided have no helpers. When God's guidance is gone, no one can substitute — human help can't replace divine direction." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "So direct your face toward the religion, inclining to truth. — Quran 30:30a", scriptureExplanation: "Face the truth. Turn toward religion with sincerity — the fitrah (natural disposition) is toward God. We're made for Him." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Adhere to the fitrah of Allah upon which He has created people. — Quran 30:30b", scriptureExplanation: "There is a natural religion. Fitrah — our original nature — is oriented toward God. True religion aligns with how we were made." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "There should be no change in the creation of Allah. — Quran 30:30c", scriptureExplanation: "Don't alter God's design. The fitrah is good as created — trying to change it leads to distortion. Acceptance of God's design is peace." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "That is the correct religion, but most people do not know. — Quran 30:30d", scriptureExplanation: "Most people don't know the right religion. Truth is accessible but not popular — the majority can be wrong. Don't follow the crowd; follow the truth." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Incline to Him and fear Him and establish prayer and do not be of those who associate partners with Him. — Quran 30:31", scriptureExplanation: "Five commands: turn, fear, pray, don't associate, don't divide. The path is clear — devotion, reverence, worship, purity, unity." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Or of those who have divided their religion and become sects, every faction rejoicing in what it has. — Quran 30:32", scriptureExplanation: "Division is a warning. Sectarianism — each group happy with its own piece — fragments the truth. Unity is God's design; division is our failure." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, Allah will not change what a people have until they change what is in themselves. — Quran 13:11 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Internal change precedes external. God transforms our circumstances when we transform our hearts — repentance is the prerequisite for renewal." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And when harm touches man, he calls upon Us. — Quran 39:49a", scriptureExplanation: "We pray when we hurt. Hardship drives us to God — which is good, but shouldn't be the only time we pray. Consistency is the goal." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Then when We grant him a favor from Us, he says, 'I have only been given it by my knowledge.' — Quran 39:49b", scriptureExplanation: "We take credit for God's gifts. When the crisis passes, we attribute the rescue to ourselves — humility in hardship becomes pride in ease." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Rather, it is a trial, but most of them do not know. — Quran 39:49c", scriptureExplanation: "Ease is also a test. Prosperity tests gratitude as much as adversity tests patience — and most fail the test of ease. Abundance is not just reward; it's examination." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Those before them said it, but what they earned did not avail them. — Quran 39:49d", scriptureExplanation: "Past nations made the same mistake. They attributed success to themselves — and it didn't save them. History is a teacher; learn from others' errors." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "So they were stricken by the evil of what they earned, and those who wronged among these will be stricken by the evil of what they earned. — Quran 39:50-51", scriptureExplanation: "Consequences follow wrongdoing. What happened before will happen again — the pattern of sin and consequence is consistent. Learn from the past." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And they will not be able to avoid it. — Quran 39:51b", scriptureExplanation: "Consequences are inescapable. The wrongdoer can't dodge the result — accountability is built into the moral order. Repentance is the only escape." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Do they not know that Allah extends provision for whom He wills and restricts it? — Quran 39:52a", scriptureExplanation: "Provision is God's to give. He expands and restricts — our job is gratitude, not comparison. What we have is exactly what He intends." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed in that are signs for a people who believe. — Quran 39:52b", scriptureExplanation: "Believers see signs in provision. The faithful recognize God's hand in abundance and scarcity — both are from Him, and both have purpose." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Say, 'O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah.' — Quran 39:53 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "No sin is beyond God's mercy. This verse is addressed to the worst sinners — and the message is hope. Despair is the only unforgivable sin." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, Allah forgives all sins. — Quran 39:53b", scriptureExplanation: "All sins are forgivable. Not some, not most — all. The only condition is repentance. God's mercy is greater than any failure." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, it is He who is the Forgiving, the Affectionate. — Quran 39:53c (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "God's names are His nature. Al-Ghafur (the Forgiving) and Ar-Ra'uf (the Affectionate) — He is defined by mercy. Forgiveness is not an act but an attribute." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And turn to Allah in repentance, all of you, O believers, that you might succeed. — Quran 24:31", scriptureExplanation: "Repentance leads to success. Turning back to God is the path to true flourishing — falah (success) follows tawbah (return). Everyone is called." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "The believers are only those who, when Allah is mentioned, their hearts become fearful. — Quran 8:2", scriptureExplanation: "Reverence is physical. The believer's heart trembles at God's mention — awe is not just intellectual but visceral. True faith is felt." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And when His verses are recited to them, it increases them in faith. — Quran 8:2b", scriptureExplanation: "Revelation increases faith. The Quran doesn't just inform — it transforms. Each reading deepens trust. The word is alive." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Upon their Lord they rely. — Quran 8:2c", scriptureExplanation: "Reliance is the mark of faith. Tawakkul — trusting God completely — is the believer's foundation. Self-reliance is replaced by God-reliance." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Those who establish prayer and spend from what We have provided them. — Quran 8:3", scriptureExplanation: "Prayer and charity define the believer. Worship upward (prayer) and care outward (charity) — both are essential. Faith without works is incomplete." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "It is those who are the believers, in truth. — Quran 8:4", scriptureExplanation: "True belief has marks. Not everyone who claims faith has it — the evidence is in prayer, charity, and reliance. Deeds verify claims." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "For them are degrees of reward from their Lord and forgiveness and noble provision. — Quran 8:4b", scriptureExplanation: "Believers are rewarded in layers. Degrees of reward — not everyone gets the same — plus forgiveness and provision. The faithful are cared for in every dimension." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, the religion in the sight of Allah is Islam. — Quran 3:19", scriptureExplanation: "Islam (submission to God) is the true religion. Not a name but a posture — surrender to the One. All true religion is submission." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And those who were given the Scripture did not differ except after knowledge had come to them. — Quran 3:19b", scriptureExplanation: "Division follows knowledge, not ignorance. People split after receiving truth — disagreement is often willful, not accidental. Knowledge increases accountability." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And whoever disbelieves in the verses of Allah, then indeed, Allah is swift in account. — Quran 3:19c", scriptureExplanation: "God's accounting is swift. Disbelief has consequences — and God's reckoning, though patient, is certain. Don't mistake delay for forgetfulness." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "So if they argue with you, say, 'I have submitted myself to Allah and so have those who follow me.' — Quran 3:20", scriptureExplanation: "Our answer is submission. When challenged, the response is simple: I've surrendered to God. Argument is replaced by testimony." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And say to those who were given the Scripture and to the unlettered, 'Have you submitted yourselves?' — Quran 3:20b", scriptureExplanation: "The question is for everyone. Scripture-holders and unlettered alike — have you submitted? The call is universal. Islam is for all." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And if they submit, they are rightly guided. — Quran 3:20c", scriptureExplanation: "Submission is guidance. Those who surrender to God are on the right path — the act of submitting IS the guidance. The path is the posture." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But if they turn away, then upon you is only the message. — Quran 3:20d", scriptureExplanation: "Our duty is delivery, not conversion. If they reject, our responsibility ends — we delivered the message. Results are God's." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And Allah is Seeing of the servants. — Quran 3:20e", scriptureExplanation: "God sees everyone. He watches both the messenger and the rejecter — nothing is hidden. His vision is comprehensive and just." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, those who disbelieve in the verses of Allah and kill the prophets without right and kill those who order justice — give them tidings of a painful punishment. — Quran 3:21", scriptureExplanation: "Injustice has consequences. Killing prophets and persecuting the just — these are the worst crimes. God's punishment is certain for the oppressors." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "They are the ones whose deeds have become worthless in this world and the Hereafter. — Quran 3:22", scriptureExplanation: "Evil deeds are ultimately worthless. What the wicked build doesn't last — their efforts are void in both worlds. Sin is its own futility." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And for them there will be no helpers. — Quran 3:22b", scriptureExplanation: "The wicked stand alone. No one can help them in the end — their alliances fail. True security comes only from God." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Have you not seen those who were given a portion of the Scripture, being invited to the Scripture of Allah that it should arbitrate between them? — Quran 3:23", scriptureExplanation: "Some reject the very Scripture they claim. Called to God's word, they turn away — selective obedience is not obedience. The test is whether we submit to what we don't prefer." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Then a party of them turns away, and they are turning away. — Quran 3:23b", scriptureExplanation: "Partial obedience is rejection. Some turn away even from their own Scripture — selective faith is no faith. Consistency is the mark of submission." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Say, 'O Allah, Owner of Sovereignty, You give sovereignty to whom You will and You take sovereignty away from whom You will.' — Quran 3:26", scriptureExplanation: "God controls power. He gives and takes authority — no one rules except by His permission. This humbles the powerful and encourages the weak." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "You honor whom You will and You humble whom You will. — Quran 3:26b", scriptureExplanation: "Honor and humility are God's to give. He elevates and lowers — our position is His decision, not our achievement. Both states are tests." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "In Your hand is all good. — Quran 3:26c", scriptureExplanation: "All good comes from God. Every blessing, every benefit — His hand holds them all. Gratitude is directed to the Source, not the channel." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, You are able to do all things. — Quran 3:26d", scriptureExplanation: "God's power is unlimited. Nothing is too hard for Him — 'all things' includes everything. Our impossibilities are His opportunities." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "You cause the night to enter the day and the day to enter the night. — Quran 3:27a", scriptureExplanation: "God controls time. The transition of night and day is His doing — even the rhythm of the cosmos is in His hands. He orders our days." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And You bring the living out of the dead and the dead out of the living. — Quran 3:27b", scriptureExplanation: "God gives life from death. This is both physical (birth) and spiritual (resurrection) — He is the source of life in every sense." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And You give provision to whom You will without account. — Quran 3:27c", scriptureExplanation: "God's provision is limitless. He gives without measure — no calculation constrains His generosity. His resources are infinite." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Let not believers take disbelievers as allies rather than believers. — Quran 3:28", scriptureExplanation: "Choose your allies wisely. Believers shouldn't prefer the company of those who reject God — alliances reveal allegiances. Loyalty matters." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And whoever does that has nothing from Allah, except that you guard yourselves against them in fear. — Quran 3:28b", scriptureExplanation: "Self-protection is allowed. Prudence in hostile environments is not betrayal — but genuine alliance with God's enemies is. Discernment is needed." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But Allah warns you of Himself, and to Allah is the return. — Quran 3:28c", scriptureExplanation: "God Himself is the warning. The ultimate consequence is facing Him — and He is the destination. Both warning and hope point to the same reality." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Say, 'Whether you conceal what is in your hearts or reveal it, Allah knows it.' — Quran 3:29", scriptureExplanation: "Nothing is hidden from God. Hearts, secrets, intentions — all are open to Him. Honesty before God is the only real honesty." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "He knows what is in the heavens and what is in the earth. — Quran 3:29b", scriptureExplanation: "God's knowledge is universal. Not just hearts but everything — heaven and earth. His omniscience is total and comprehensive." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And Allah is competent over all things. — Quran 3:29c", scriptureExplanation: "God's power matches His knowledge. He knows everything and can do anything — omniscience and omnipotence together. He is fully God." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "The Day every soul will find what it has done of good present and what it has done of evil, it will wish that between it and that evil were a great distance. — Quran 3:30", scriptureExplanation: "The Day of Judgment is personal. Each soul sees its own deeds — good and bad. The wish for distance from evil shows the weight of accountability." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And Allah warns you of Himself, but Allah is Kind to His servants. — Quran 3:30b", scriptureExplanation: "Warning and kindness together. God warns because He cares — His severity is an expression of His compassion. True love includes warning." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Say, 'If you love Allah, then follow me, and Allah will love you and forgive you your sins.' — Quran 3:31", scriptureExplanation: "Love of God is shown by following the Prophet. Not just feeling but action — following is the proof of love. And God's love follows our following." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And Allah is Forgiving and Merciful. — Quran 3:31b", scriptureExplanation: "God's response to our following is forgiveness. He doesn't just tolerate us — He loves us back. The relationship is reciprocal." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Say, 'Obey Allah and the Messenger.' But if they turn away — then indeed, Allah does not like the disbelievers. — Quran 3:32", scriptureExplanation: "Obedience is the test of love. Those who turn away from obedience don't truly love God — and He doesn't love the defiant. Action validates affection." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, Allah chose Adam and Noah and the family of Abraham and the family of Imran over the worlds. — Quran 3:33", scriptureExplanation: "God's choice is purposeful. He selected specific people for specific roles — selection is not favoritism but mission. Chosenness comes with responsibility." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Descendants, some of them from others. And Allah is Hearing and Knowing. — Quran 3:34", scriptureExplanation: "Prophetic lineage is connected. The chosen are related — a family line of faith. God works through generations." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, the most noble of you in the sight of Allah is the most righteous of you. — Quran 49:13", scriptureExplanation: "Nobility is based on righteousness, not race or wealth. In God's sight, the best person is the most God-conscious — not the most powerful or rich. True hierarchy is spiritual." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "O you who have believed, seek help through patience and prayer. Indeed, Allah is with the patient. — Quran 2:153", scriptureExplanation: "Patience and prayer are the believer's tools. And God is with the patient — His presence is the reward of endurance. He doesn't leave us alone in the wait." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And do not say about those who are killed in the way of Allah, 'They are dead.' Rather, they are alive, but you do not perceive. — Quran 2:154", scriptureExplanation: "Martyrs are alive. What looks like death is actually life — we can't perceive it, but it's real. The next life is more alive than this one." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And We will surely test you with something of fear and hunger and a loss of wealth and lives and fruits, but give good tidings to the patient. — Quran 2:155", scriptureExplanation: "Tests are certain. Fear, hunger, loss — all are coming. But the patient receive good news. Hardship is not punishment but preparation." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Who, when disaster strikes them, say, 'Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return.' — Quran 2:156", scriptureExplanation: "The believer's response to disaster: belonging and returning. 'We are God's and we go back to God' — this is the perspective that transforms suffering into surrender." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Those are the ones upon whom are blessings from their Lord and mercy. And it is those who are the rightly guided. — Quran 2:157", scriptureExplanation: "Blessings and mercy follow the patient. Those who say 'we belong to God' receive His blessing and mercy — and they are guided. Surrender leads to everything." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, the patient will be given their reward without account. — Quran 39:10", scriptureExplanation: "Patience is rewarded beyond measure. 'Without account' — no limit, no calculation. God's reward for endurance is infinite. The wait is worth it." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Say, 'O My servants who have believed, fear your Lord. For those who do good in this world is good, and the earth of Allah is spacious.' — Quran 39:10 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Fear God and do good — and the reward is both here and hereafter. The earth is spacious — there's room for the faithful. Don't feel trapped; God makes space." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, the patient will be given their reward without account. — Quran 39:10b (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Unlimited reward for patience. God doesn't measure His gift to the patient — it overflows. Endurance is the currency of infinite return." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Say: 'Nothing will happen to us except what Allah has decreed for us; He is our protector.' — Quran 9:51", scriptureExplanation: "Nothing happens outside God's decree. What He wills, happens; what He doesn't, doesn't. And He is our protector — we are safe within His will, even in hardship." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And upon Allah let the believers rely. — Quran 9:51b", scriptureExplanation: "Reliance is the believer's response. Knowing God is in control, we trust — tawakkul. Peace comes from surrender, not from understanding." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And whoever relies upon Allah — then He is sufficient for him. — Quran 65:3 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "God is enough. When we rely on Him, He is sufficient — nothing else is needed. Tawakkul replaces all other dependencies with one: God alone." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, Allah will accomplish His purpose. Allah has already set for everything a decreed term. — Quran 65:3 (alt. trans.)", scriptureExplanation: "God's purpose is accomplished. Nothing can stop it — and everything has its appointed time. Patience trusts God's timing, not our own." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And whoever is conscious of Allah — He will make for him a way out. — Quran 65:2", scriptureExplanation: "Taqwa opens doors. God-consciousness creates an exit from difficulty — not always the exit we expect, but always the right one. Reverence leads to rescue." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And will provide for him from where he does not expect. — Quran 65:3 (alt. trans. 2)", scriptureExplanation: "Provision comes from unexpected sources. When we trust God, He provides in surprising ways — our expectation limits us; His provision doesn't." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And whoever places his trust in Allah — He is sufficient for him. — Quran 65:3 (alt. trans. 3)", scriptureExplanation: "Sufficiency is God's gift to the trusting. He doesn't just help — He IS the help. Trust transforms insufficiency into sufficiency." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, Allah is with those who are righteous and those who do good. — Quran 16:128 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "God's presence follows goodness. He is with the righteous and the doers of good — not just the believers in name. Practice attracts presence." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins. — Quran 39:53 (alt. 2)", scriptureExplanation: "Despair is the enemy. God's mercy is bigger than any sin — the only unforgivable sin is despair of His forgiveness. Hope is the door to grace." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, it is He who is the Forgiving, the Affectionate. — Quran 39:53 (alt. 2b)", scriptureExplanation: "God's nature is mercy. Al-Ghafur, Ar-Ra'uf — forgiving and affectionate. These aren't actions He does but attributes He is. Mercy is His identity." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And He is the One who sends down rain after they had despaired and spreads His mercy. — Quran 42:28", scriptureExplanation: "God sends rain after despair. When hope is gone, He provides — His mercy arrives at the darkest moment. Don't give up before the rain." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And He is the Guardian, the Praiseworthy. — Quran 42:28b", scriptureExplanation: "God is our Guardian (Wali) and Praiseworthy (Hameed). He protects and deserves praise — both His care and His character are perfect." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And of His signs is the creation of the heavens and the earth and the living creatures He dispersed in them. — Quran 42:29", scriptureExplanation: "Life in the cosmos is a sign. God created and dispersed creatures — life is His signature. The universe is not empty but inhabited by His design." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And He is able to gather them when He wills. — Quran 42:29b", scriptureExplanation: "God can gather all creation. The Gathering is coming — He has the power to bring everything together. The Day of Judgment is within His capability." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And whatever strikes you of disaster — it is for what your hands have earned; but He pardons much. — Quran 42:30", scriptureExplanation: "Consequences are earned, but God pardons much. What we suffer is often our own doing — but God forgives more than He punishes. Mercy exceeds justice." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And you will not cause failure upon the earth. — Quran 42:31", scriptureExplanation: "We can't escape God. Running from Him is futile — the earth is His, and we can't outrun the One who made it. Surrender is the only sensible option." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And you have not besides Allah any protector or helper. — Quran 42:31b", scriptureExplanation: "God is the only real protector. No human, no institution, no wealth can truly help — only He can. Independence from God is an illusion." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And of His signs are the ships in the sea, like banners. — Quran 42:32", scriptureExplanation: "Even ships are a sign. Human technology sailing on God's ocean — our abilities are built on His creation. Every achievement rests on His foundation." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "If He willed, He could still the wind, and they would remain motionless on its surface. — Quran 42:33", scriptureExplanation: "God controls the wind. The same wind that moves ships can be stilled — our progress depends on His permission. Success is not self-made." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed in that are signs for everyone patient and grateful. — Quran 42:33b", scriptureExplanation: "Signs are for the patient and grateful. Two qualities reveal God's messages: endurance in hardship and gratitude in ease. Both open our eyes." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Or He could destroy them for what they earned, but He pardons much. — Quran 42:34", scriptureExplanation: "God could destroy us for our sins — but He pardons much. His restraint is mercy. Every moment of existence is a gift we haven't earned." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But those who dispute concerning Our signs will know that there is no place of escape. — Quran 42:35", scriptureExplanation: "Arguing with God's signs is futile. The disputatious will learn — too late — that there's no escape. Humility now prevents regret later." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "So whatever you have been given — it is but enjoyment of the worldly life. — Quran 42:36", scriptureExplanation: "Worldly blessings are temporary. What we have now is just for this life — it's not the real reward. Don't cling to what doesn't last." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But what is with Allah is better and more lasting for those who have believed and upon their Lord rely. — Quran 42:36b", scriptureExplanation: "God's reward is better and eternal. What He gives is both superior and permanent — the Hereafter outshines this life in quality and duration." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And those who avoid the major sins and immoralities, and when they are angry, they forgive. — Quran 42:37", scriptureExplanation: "Forgiveness in anger is a mark of faith. Avoiding major sins is expected — but forgiving while angry is extraordinary. Self-control in emotion is the test." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And those who have responded to their Lord and established prayer and whose affair is determined among themselves by consultation. — Quran 42:38", scriptureExplanation: "Consultation (shura) is a mark of the faithful. Decisions are made together — not by dictation but by discussion. Community requires collaboration." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And those who spend from what We have provided them. — Quran 42:38b", scriptureExplanation: "Generosity is a sign of faith. The believers share what they've been given — wealth is not hoarded but distributed. Charity is worship." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And those who, when tyranny strikes them, they defend themselves. — Quran 42:39", scriptureExplanation: "Self-defense is allowed. The believer doesn't seek conflict but responds to oppression — standing up to tyranny is not just permitted but commanded." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And the retribution for an evil is an evil like it. But whoever pardons and makes reconciliation — his reward is from Allah. — Quran 42:40", scriptureExplanation: "Forgiveness is rewarded by God. Equal retribution is allowed — but pardon is better. The one who forgives receives their reward from God Himself." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, He does not like the wrongdoers. — Quran 42:40b", scriptureExplanation: "God dislikes oppressors. Those who initiate harm are detested by Him — but those who respond with forgiveness are loved. Justice and mercy together." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And whoever avenges himself after having been wronged — those have not upon them any cause for blame. — Quran 42:41", scriptureExplanation: "The wronged may seek justice. Self-defense after oppression is blameless — but forgiveness is still better. Justice is allowed; mercy is preferred." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "The cause for blame is only against those who wrong people and tyrannize on the earth without right. — Quran 42:42", scriptureExplanation: "Blame is for the initiator. Those who start the oppression are at fault — not those who respond. God distinguishes between aggression and defense." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But whoever is patient and forgives — indeed, that is of the matters requiring determination. — Quran 42:43", scriptureExplanation: "Patience and forgiveness require great strength. It's not weakness but resolve — 'determination' (azm) is the word. True courage forgives." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And whoever Allah sends astray — there is no protector for him after that. — Quran 42:44", scriptureExplanation: "Without God's guidance, we're lost. He is the only guide — and if He withdraws, no one can replace Him. Don't persist in what removes His guidance." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And you will see the wrongdoers, when they see the punishment, saying, 'Is there for return any way?' — Quran 42:44b", scriptureExplanation: "Regret comes too late. The wrongdoer wants to return when it's too late — the door was open before. Don't wait until consequences arrive to repent." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And you will see them being exposed to the Fire, humbled from humiliation, looking from a hidden place. — Quran 42:45", scriptureExplanation: "The wicked will see their fate. Exposed, humbled, hiding — the proud are brought low. What they built cannot protect them." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And those who believed and did righteous deeds will be in a green meadow of Paradise, having whatever they desire from their Lord. — Quran 42:22 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "The believers' reward is lush and personal. A green meadow, whatever they desire — Paradise is both beautiful and tailored. God's reward exceeds our imagination." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "That is the great bounty. — Quran 42:22b", scriptureExplanation: "God's reward is 'the great bounty' — not a small gift but an overwhelming one. What He gives is beyond what we could ask or think." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "This is what Allah promises to His servants who fear Him. — Quran 42:22c (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "God's promises are for the God-conscious. Fear (taqwa) is the condition — not terror but reverence. Those who revere God receive His promise." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Say: 'I do not ask of you for it any reward, but love in kin.' — Quran 42:23", scriptureExplanation: "The Prophet asked only for love. Not wealth, not power — just love among kin. The currency of prophethood is relationship, not reward." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And whoever commits a good deed — We will increase for him in good. — Quran 42:23b", scriptureExplanation: "God multiplies good. One good deed brings increased reward — His generosity compounds. Every act of kindness is an investment." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, Allah is Forgiving and Grateful. — Quran 42:23c", scriptureExplanation: "God is 'Grateful' (Shakur) — He appreciates our small efforts. Even our modest good deeds are noticed and rewarded. The Creator is thankful to the created." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Or do they say, 'He has invented about Allah a lie?' But if Allah willed, He could seal over your heart. — Quran 42:24", scriptureExplanation: "God protects truth. If He willed, He could seal hearts — but He allows truth to remain. The Prophet doesn't lie; God authenticates His message." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And Allah eliminates falsehood and establishes the truth by His words. — Quran 42:24b", scriptureExplanation: "Truth wins. God eliminates falsehood and establishes truth — not by our effort but by His word. The outcome is certain." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, He is Knowing of that within the breasts. — Quran 42:24c", scriptureExplanation: "God knows what's in the heart. Not just what we say but what we feel — He reads the breast. Sincerity is known to Him, even when hidden from others." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And it is He who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons misdeeds, and He knows what you do. — Quran 42:25", scriptureExplanation: "God accepts repentance and pardons. Two gifts: He receives our return and forgives our wrong — and He knows everything we've done. Mercy with full knowledge." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And He answers those who have believed and done righteous deeds, and He increases them from His bounty. — Quran 42:26", scriptureExplanation: "God answers and increases. He responds to the faithful — and then gives more. His generosity doesn't stop at answering; it overflows." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But the disbelievers — for them is a severe punishment. — Quran 42:26b", scriptureExplanation: "Disbelief has consequences. While believers receive increase, disbelievers face severity — the contrast is intentional. Choices matter." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And if Allah were to extend provision for His servants, they would rebel on the earth. — Quran 42:27", scriptureExplanation: "Too much can corrupt. Unlimited provision would lead to rebellion — God's measured giving is actually mercy. Less can be more." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "But He sends down according to what is due. — Quran 42:27b", scriptureExplanation: "God gives what's right. Not too much, not too little — exactly what's due. His provision is perfectly calibrated to our need and our character." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "Indeed, He is, of His servants, Acquainted and Seeing. — Quran 42:27c", scriptureExplanation: "God knows each servant individually. He's not a distant provider but a personal one — acquainted and seeing. His provision is personal." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And it is He who sends down the rain after they had despaired and spreads His mercy. — Quran 42:28 (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "Rain after despair is mercy. When hope is gone, God provides — His timing is perfect. The darkest moment precedes the dawn." },
  { category: "muslim", scripture: "And He is the Guardian, the Praiseworthy. — Quran 42:28b (alt.)", scriptureExplanation: "God guards and deserves praise. He protects His servants and is worthy of all worship — both His care and His character invite adoration." },
];